course: dictionary
lesson: 10205
title: Tipsy and other words for merry
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Tipsy is an informal word, so you will hear it in relaxed, everyday talk more than in school writing. It means slightly drunk from drinking alcohol: a bit happy and unsteady, but not very drunk. Alcohol is for adults only, and children must never drink it.
explain: Look at the clues in the sentence. «Picture a wedding in Galway: Auntie Siobhan giggles that she is a bit tipsy.» Giggling tells you she feels silly and happy, and the wedding tells you she has had a little to drink. Ask: what word would fit here? Then put slightly drunk in its place and check that the sentence still makes sense.
explain: Some people use a softer word instead of drunk, to be polite or to joke. They might say someone is «merry», «tipsy» or has had «one too many». Tipsy is one of the lightest of these words. Plainly drunk is much stronger and more serious.
fact: Tipsy means slightly drunk from alcohol: a bit happy and unsteady, but not very drunk.
fact: Tipsy is an informal word, so it belongs in chatty, everyday talk.
fact: Alcohol is for adults only. Children must never drink it.
fact: «Merry» and «one too many» are polite or joking ways to say someone has had some alcohol.
fact: Synonyms can have different strengths: tipsy is light, while plainly drunk is much stronger.
exercise: «Auntie Siobhan giggles that she is a bit tipsy.» What does tipsy mean? | Very angry and shouting loudly | *Slightly drunk from alcohol, a bit happy and unsteady | Tired and ready for bed | Hungry and wanting dinner
exercise: In polite talk, which word can mean a little drunk? | *Merry | Angry | Hungry | Sleepy
exercise: Is tipsy a formal or informal word? | Formal, used in official letters | Scientific, used in laboratory reports | Old-fashioned, used in poems | *Informal, used in relaxed everyday talk
test: Which is true about alcohol? | Children can drink a little at a party | It is always a safe drink for children | *Children should never drink it, because it is for adults only
test: Which word means the strongest kind of drunk? | Merry | Chatty | *Plainly drunk | Tipsy
exam: Which sentence uses tipsy correctly? | *After one drink at the wedding, Auntie Siobhan felt a bit tipsy | Tipsy means very tall and thin | The hot sun made the path tipsy | The train was tipsy on the track
